      "year": 2026,
      "abstract": "\n \n The paper analyzes the structural unity between\n Wissenschaftslehre\n and\n Staatslehre\n in Fichte\u2019s late works, emphasizing their convergence in a philosophical project that integrates speculative insight and political transformation. The multiplicity of expositions of the\n Wissenschaftslehre\n is interpreted as an essential feature of its identity, grounded in the dynamic self-manifestation of the Absolute through consciousness. Philosophical insight (\n Einsicht\n ) becomes the medium through which theory is transfigured into life and action. The\n Staatslehre\n introduces Christ as the absolute historical fact that enables a shift from a pre-modern political theology based on miracles and coercion to a post-Christian order grounded in freedom and rational self-determination. Sovereignty, traditionally legitimized by revelation or contract, is reconfigured as the unfolding of transcendental intelligence within a community. The dissolution of theological\u2013political authority culminates in a constitutional model in which reason itself governs. In this framework, the\n Wissenschaftslehre\n emerges as both speculative doctrine and political constitution, replacing faith with self-conscious insight as the foundation of political legitimacy.\n",
