      ],
      "year": 2023,
      "abstract": "\nThe second edition of the 1804 Wissenschaftslehre purports to be a self-development of rationality, a rational knowledge of knowledge. The \u2018rational\u2019 refers a) to the mind and b) to a specific form of objectification called evidence of \u2018reason\u2019. In the first part of the lecture series, Fichte refers to the entire course as \u2018a doctrine of reason and truth\u2019 (15th lecture, ibid., p. 150), and second, as a \u2018doctrine of appearance and illusion\u2019, but one that is indeed true and is grounded in truth (15th lecture, ibid., pp. 150\u2013151). The theory of appearances is a second ascent: this is because in the facticity of an appearance, the genesis of a certain reason-consequent relationship can be asserted. The synthesis of reason and freedom are thus mutually dependent in the true image of being (\u2018Bild-Wirklichkeit\u2019) and in the knowledge of a genetic relationship. The focus of the investigation is the 27th lecture, but other lectures are consulted for understanding.",
